      "id": "magpie",
      "name": "Magpie",
      "protocol_version": "0",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "category": "ai",
      "placements": [
        "menubar"
      ],
      "open_mode": "flyout",
      "window_style": "standard",
      "description": "Control magpie from the menu bar: switch agents' models, connect agents, and watch allowances.",
      "icon": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,",
      "license": "AGPL-3.0-only",
      "homepage": "https://github.com/yetone/magpie",
      "docs": "Connects to a magpie you run elsewhere, such as on a server.\n\n1. Open magpie's web page from the link it prints (magpie web, or Settings › Network and sharing › Browser access in the app). The link looks like http://HOST:PORT/?k=KEY.\n2. Put http://HOST:PORT into Magpie URL and KEY into Web Key.\n\nThe key grants full control of that magpie, so keep it private. Plain HTTP is allowed for Magpie URL only, since magpie web usually runs on a home network or tailnet without HTTPS. Which sections the panel shows, its language and the menu bar text are in these settings too.",
      "file": "magpie/magpie.bar",
      "sha256": "54696bec130e46afdade9f7bcecb6ba3d1a61dbc6c014890c1aadf356c0bbf82"
    }
  ]
